# Inline: answering "find me a flight to Madrid" inside the chat feed.
# One surface, one job — the options and a way to pick one.
surface("inline-7")
# That id is the one this turn was given ("Draw into surface ..."), never an
# earlier card's. A card already answered is the record of that answer, and a
# root drawn onto it takes the place of what the traveler picked from.
heading = Text("Outbound · JFK → MAD · Sun 12 Apr", variant="h3")
# One call, drawn *before* search_flights is called. The lookup files its rows
# at /flights and this reads them: bound, labelled, pressable, however many
# come back. Writing a FlightOption per result instead is three hundred tokens
# the traveler waits through, and the one part of the turn that can disagree
# with what was actually found.
fares = Flights("Outbound · JFK → MAD · Sun 12 Apr", "/trip/selectedOutbound")
note = Text("Prices are per traveler, round trip.")
root = Column([heading, fares, note])
